<title>USA: Security flaw possible in smart cards - NY Times.</title>
<headline>Security flaw possible in smart cards - NY Times.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Electronic cash cards now in use in Europe and undergoing testing in certain U.S. cities have a potential security flaw that allows counterfeiters to duplicate the cards' values, the New York Times reported on Thursday.</p>
<p>Computer scientists at Bell Communications Research said sophisticated criminals might be able to manipulate computer chips embedded in the cards, called &quot;smart cards&quot;, to make a counterfeit copy of a legitimate card.</p>
<p>Chase Manhattan Corp, Citicorp's Citibank, Master Card International Inc and Visa International Inc plan a test of smart cards with 50,000 customers in New York City later this year, the article said.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk  (212) 859-1610</p>
